={{ $('Reconcile Order Confirmation').item.json.detail }}

Their words: {{ $('Reconcile Order Confirmation').item.json.summary }}

The line is marked at risk in Purchase orders, with their date on it, so tomorrow's run plans around what is really coming rather than what we asked for. What it cannot do is find the stock somewhere else.

=A supplier wrote back and the workflow did not act on it alone.

From:    {{ $json.from }}
Subject: {{ $json.subject }}

Why you have it: {{ $json.why }}

{{ $json.detail }}

What they wrote, with our own email underneath it taken off:
{{ $json.fresh_text }}

Nothing has been written to the sheet.

=A run of the replenishment workflow stopped with an error.

Error:     {{ $json.execution.error.message }}
At node:   {{ $json.execution.lastNodeExecuted }}
Execution: {{ $json.execution.url }}

Orders are written to the Purchase orders tab as each one is sent, so anything already emailed is in the pipeline and the next run counts it. What a failure loses is the rest of the morning, not what it had already done.
